jq("j-r-flatten", "Flatten a Nested Array", "HARD", T, "A nested array is written like `[1,[2,3],[4,[5]]]`. Write a recursive method that walks the text and prints the numbers in order on one line, separated by spaces.", "One line without spaces.", "The flat numbers.", "At most 200 characters",
   'List<String> out = new ArrayList<>();\nflatten(s, 0, out);\nSystem.out.println(String.join(" ", out));', ["[1,[2,3],[4,[5]]]", "[7]", "[[1],[2],[3]]", "[[[[9]]]]", "[10,[20,[30,[40]]],50]"], [("String", "s")],
   members='static int flatten(String s, int i, List<String> out) {\n    i++;\n    while (s.charAt(i) != \']\') {\n        char c = s.charAt(i);\n        if (c == \'[\') i = flatten(s, i, out);\n        else if (c == \',\') i++;\n        else {\n            int j = i;\n            while (Character.isDigit(s.charAt(j))) j++;\n            out.add(s.substring(i, j));\n            i = j;\n        }\n    }\n    return i + 1;\n}')
